>>
Rule 1 (input must be a matrix or batch of matrices)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 2
>>
Rule 2 (out tensor matches input dtype and shape)
{v_1 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 2 ∧ ndim(v_3) = ndim(v_1) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_3, i) = shape(v_1, i) ∧ dtype_(v_3) = dtype_(v_1)
>>
Rule 3 (diagonal index within the extent of the last two dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 2 ∧ v_2 ≥ 0 - shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 2) ∧ v_2 ≤ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1)
>>
Rule 4 (out must be a tensor, not a float)
{v_3 : tensor} |= ndim(v_3) ≥ 0
